{"thought":"The `dumps` function checks if the data is a `Mapping` and then converts it to a dictionary before calling `item(data, _sort_keys=sort_keys).as_string()`. This suggests that the order of keys in the dictionary may not be preserved if the dictionary is created from an unordered collection. I will now create a test that reproduces the issue described in the issue report.","tool":"run_test","args":{"source":"import tomlkit

def test_scalar_captured_by_dictionary():
    doc = tomlkit.loads("""a.b = 1\n""")
    doc["a"]["c"] = {}
    doc["z"] = 2
    result = tomlkit.dumps(doc)
    expected = """a.b = 1\n\n[a.c]\nz = 2\n"""
    assert result == expected, f'Expected: {expected}, but got: {result}'
"}}
